"user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T07:00:41-07:00","id":1540081,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time seeing the full difference <i>in nature</i> compared to the Nephilim. I can see that the Battleground Angels are more of a militia than an army, of course, but do they basically pick up any Outcast no matter the origin of their Curse ? Or do they select peoples than can trace their Curse to those beings of the Outside who fights constantly on the Battlegrounds ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T11:21:06-07:00","id":1540092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1540046-curseborne-the-outcasts-2-the-battleground-angels?p=1540081#post1540081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time seeing the full difference <i>in nature</i> compared to the Nephilim. I can see that the Battleground Angels are more of a militia than an army, of course, but do they basically pick up any Outcast no matter the origin of their Curse ? Or do they select peoples than can trace their Curse to those beings of the Outside who fights constantly on the Battlegrounds ?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Nephilim are travelers. They are information brokers, explorers, and smugglers. They go into Outsides and Battlegrounds as a means to an end, but they don't want to stay there and fight people. Battleground Angels are the scrappy Outcasts who refuse to accept their lot in life. They want to take the fight to the archons, they want to regain their place in the Outsides, and they are building an army to do it. They will absolutely accept anyone and everyone who is an Outcast, regardless of how they got their curse. You can't raise an army by being too picky about who your soldiers are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T19:19:00-07:00","id":1540116,"title":"","content":"I think that the &quot;families&quot; of the Outcast give me more of an impression of a club or alliance than actual families, and that goes for the Nephilim as well.<br /> <br /> The Primals did gave a strong sense of each family being that, a lineage of cursed people, your character may be on board with them or not, but can't really pretend they're not blood.<br /> <br /> Now with the Outcasts I get the feeling of something akin to the Lost: unrelated people whose only common thread is the nature of their parents, but not really the vibe of family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T23:15:43-07:00","id":1540121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1540046-curseborne-the-outcasts-2-the-battleground-angels?p=1540116#post1540116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the &quot;families&quot; of the Outcast give me more of an impression of a club or alliance than actual families, and that goes for the Nephilim as well.<br /> <br /> The Primals did gave a strong sense of each family being that, a lineage of cursed people, your character may be on board with them or not, but can't really pretend they're not blood.<br /> <br /> Now with the Outcasts I get the feeling of something akin to the Lost: unrelated people whose only common thread is the nature of their parents, but not really the vibe of family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be onto something here. I'm just reading the French version of Changelings The Lost' corebook and there is definitely a similar vibe to what we know of the Outcasts in that book. Which is great as Changelings and Demons are perhaps my favourite splats in CofD.<br /> <br /> Still, I can't wait to learn more about the Oucasts third example of &quot;lineage&quot; so to speak. And the rules to create our own, hopefully, which would be neat.<br /> <br /> And as I said, the Archons. What are they ? What links them together as a sort of similar kind of entities ? So many questions I can't wait to see answered !<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}